[00:00] [scene:SCENE]
VISUAL: ComfyUI update process shown in a Windows Explorer window.
AUDIO: 'MiniMax H3 has been released, and it&nbsp; is capable of generating text-to-video,&nbsp;&nbsp; image-to-video, and reference-to-video. So, in&nbsp; this video, I\'ll run the model on my RTX 5060&nbsp;&nbsp; Ti 16 GB to see how well it performs&nbsp; and generate a few videos. I\'ll first&nbsp;&nbsp; update ComfyUI to the nightly version. If you\'re using the stable version,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[00:16] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'run the file shown below to update it. In the&nbsp; Templates section, select MiniMax H3 to filter&nbsp;&nbsp; the workflows. We have three workflows here. These workflows require an API to run,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[00:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'so you\'ll need to purchase some credits to&nbsp; use them. These three workflows, however,&nbsp;&nbsp; run completely locally. Let\'s begin with the&nbsp; text-to-video workflow. The links to all the&nbsp;&nbsp; required files are provided inside the workflow,&nbsp; but first I want to check the file sizes.'

[00:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'The BF16 model won\'t even fit on a flagship&nbsp; graphics card. You will need a workstation&nbsp;&nbsp; graphics card, so I will be using the smaller&nbsp; models. There are two types of models here. This&nbsp;&nbsp; one is the Reference-to-Video-Audio&nbsp; model, and the one above it is the&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[01:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'First-and-Last-Frame-to-Video-Audio model. The&nbsp; same model is also used for text-to-video when&nbsp;&nbsp; no image is provided. Save both of these&nbsp; files in the diffusion_models folder. I\'ll&nbsp;&nbsp; download the remaining files directly from the&nbsp; workflow since they are the smallest recommended&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[01:17] [scene:UI]
VISUAL: ComfyUI interface showing a "Resolution Selector" node with aspect ratio, megapixels, and multiple settings.
AUDIO: 'versions. Even a 12 GB RTX 3060 can generate&nbsp; videos using these large models in ComfyUI,&nbsp;&nbsp; but the generation time isn\'t very practical.&nbsp; It completely depends on your patience. The&nbsp;&nbsp;'

